Source: rustyssl
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: rustyssl developers <rustyssl@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), gcc, binutils
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/zebra-rs/rustyssl
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: rustyssl
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: memory-safe drop-in replacement for OpenSSL's libraries
 rustyssl reimplements libcrypto.so.3 and libssl.so.3 in Rust with OpenSSL 3's ABI,
 and the openssl command-line tool. This package installs them side by side with
 the system's OpenSSL, under /usr/lib/<arch>/rustyssl; run "rustyssl-select rustyssl"
 to make every program use them, and "rustyssl-select system" to go back.
